If you're looking for still looking for judges, may I suggest Kevin Coyne, Columbia's resident narrative guru. His classes have by far the longest waiting lists in the entire school of journalistm and the students he churns out will never look at a story the same way again. He also writes a weekly column about New Jersey for the New York Times. Even if you don't give a damn about Jersey, it's tough not to read. Just a thought. 
